ble="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[115,661][964,1764]"><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.widget.ScrollView" package="com.londkirs.antigravityremote" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="true" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[115,661][964,1764]"><node index="0" text='ON THIS PHONE (native)&#10;&#10;1. Tap "Install agy". The app downloads Google&apos;s official Android build of the Antigravity CLI and checks its SHA-512 checksum.&#10;2. Tap "Start Antigravity". agy starts in the built-in terminal in ~/projects.&#10;3. Sign in: agy opens Google sign-in in Chrome. After you approve, Chrome returns to agy automatically. If nothing opens, tap "Open" on the blue banner.&#10;4. Agents keep running in the background (see the notification). Use the menu for more sessions or a plain shell.&#10;&#10;Needs a 64-bit ARM phone. The desktop editor (GUI) does not run on Android, only the agent CLI.&#10;&#10;OPTION 1: Official Remote Control (recommended)&#10;&#10;1. On your computer, open Antigravity → Settings (Ctrl+, / Cmd+,).&#10;2. Turn on "Enable Remote Control" (Application or Account section, depending on the version). In the CLI: agy --remote-control, or /remote-control inside a session.&#10;3. Keep the computer awake and Antigravity open.&#10;4. In this app tap "Antigravity Remote Control (official)" and sign in with the SAME Google account.&#10;5. Pick your computer in the instance switcher.&#10;&#10;Tip: When Antigravity shows an "Open in Remote Control" QR code, scan it with the phone camera. The link opens in this app.&#10;&#10;If Google refuses to sign in inside the app, use the "Chrome" button. Sign-in inside Chrome always works.&#10;&#10;OPTION 2: Your own bridge&#10;Any web address that exposes your computer works: code-server, a noVNC remote desktop, an open-source Antigravity mobile bridge, or a Cloudflare / Tailscale tunnel. Tap "Add connection" and enter its address.&#10;&#10;With Remote Control the agents run on your computer.' resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.londkirs.antigravityremote" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[115,661][964,1764]" /></node></node><node index="2" text="" resource-id="" class="android.widget.LinearLayout" package="com.londkirs.antigravityremote" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[115,1801][964,1922]"><node index="0" text="Copy" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.londkirs.antigravityremote" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[131,1801][303,1922]" /><node index="1" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.londkirs.antigravityremote" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[303,1861][766,1862]" /><node index="2" text="Close" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.londkirs.antigravityremote" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[782,1801][964,1922]" /></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>